Data directory creation relies on umask for permissions rather than an explicit chmod
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/argmin-security-review-2026-06-23-m4
Criticality: medium (attack path: medium)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in 63423a0a.

The fix added a shared storage data-directory preparation helper in `crates/storage/src/data_dir.rs`. Missing data directories are created with mode `0700`; existing non-world-writable directories such as `0755` or `0775` are tightened to `0700`; existing world-writable directories such as `0777` fail closed before startup continues.

The helper is now used by the standalone storage-node data-dir lock path, embedded local-cluster node directory preparation, `LocalStorageNode::open`, and `SharedStorageNode::open_with_default_ec_shape`. This covers both standalone storage-node startup and the local frontend path that creates `ARGMIN_DATA_DIR/node-000N` directories.

Regression coverage was added for the helper itself, storage-node bind behavior, and embedded local-cluster behavior. The tests cover creation as `0700`, tightening existing readable directories to `0700`, and rejecting existing world-writable data directories.

